<facsimile><graphic url="https://www.e-manuscripta.ch/i3f/v20/1079089/manifest"/></facsimile><text><body><div type="letter">
<pb facs="1079090" n="1"/>
  <opener>Viro Illustrissimo et Celeberrimo
      <lb/><choice><abbr>Johan.</abbr><expan>Johanni</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-118509969" type="person">Bernoulli</rs> <choice><abbr>P.</abbr><expan>Petrus</expan></choice> Antonius <rs key="pers_DE-588-102552517" type="person">Michelotti</rs>
      <lb/><abbr>S. P. D.</abbr></opener>
  <p><lb/>Frustra responsion<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> hactenus a Te Vir <choice><abbr>Illustriss.</abbr><expan>Illustrissime</expan></choice>
      <lb/>expectavi ad meas <rs key="B_991170515151705501" type="letter">litteras</rs>, quas ad Te dedi <date when="1719-09-15">ante
      <lb/>dies duos et viginti</date> perque <rs key="place_VER-tirola" type="place">Tyrolim</rs> istuc velo<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>citer transmisi. Illis <rs key="B_991170515151705501" type="letter">litteris</rs> Te certior<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> facieb<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice>
      <lb/>me per <rs key="place_GEO-3173435" type="place">Mediolan<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs> celeritate Tabellarii ad
      <lb/>Te misisse me<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> <rs key="biblio_M3G2JA79" type="biblio">Dissertation<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> de Separatio<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>ne Fluidor<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> in Corpore Animali</rs><note type="editorial" resp="SG">Im <rs type="letter" key="B_991170515150805501">Brief</rs> vom 17. Mai 1720 berichtet Michelotti, dass <rs type="person" key="pers_DE-588-117589144">Nicolaus II Bernoulli</rs> ihm das Manuskript zusammen mit den Anmerkungen Johann I Bernoullis zurückbrachte. Der weitere Verbleib der Handschrift ist bislang nicht nachgewiesen.</note> ut faveres
      <lb/>eam perlegere, atque corrigere; pr<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice>terea
      <lb/>Te rogabam ut subito responderes num
      <lb/>illam ips<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> <rs key="biblio_M3G2JA79" type="biblio">Dissertation<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice></rs> accepisses. Ante
      <lb/>quindecim dies a Domina Marchionissa
      <lb/><rs key="pers_DE-588-1221330748" type="person">Loaysa Butintrochi</rs> certior factus sum ips<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice>
      <lb/>meam <rs key="biblio_M3G2JA79" type="biblio">Dissertationem</rs> a semetipsa <rs key="place_GEO-3173435" type="place">Me<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>diolano</rs>, <rs key="place_GEO-2661604" type="place">Basileam</rs> per Tabellari<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> ad Te
      <lb/>fuisse transmiss<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice>; quare spero quod ill<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice>
      <lb/>jam acceperis. Nollem ut <rs key="biblio_M3G2JA79" type="biblio">Dissertatio</rs> periret,
      <lb/>quare Te obsecro ut sine ulla mora me cer<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>tior<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> facias, sive ill<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> acceperis, sive non:
      <lb/>ista enim res vehementer me turbat. Poteris
      <lb/>qu<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice>rere, et omni uti diligentia istuc ut inve<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>nias ips<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> meam <rs key="biblio_M3G2JA79" type="biblio">Dissertation<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice></rs>, qu<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice> tel<choice><orig><g ref="#ahat">â</g></orig><reg>a</reg></choice>
      <lb/>cera illinita est obtecta, habetque signum
      <lb/>fact<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> a Clarissimo <rs key="pers_DE-588-119166895" type="person">Agnato</rs> Tuo hujuscemodi<supplied>:</supplied>
      <lb/>A Monsieur, Monsieur Jean Bernoulli Professeur
<pb facs="1079091" n="2"/>
      <lb/>tres Celebre de Matematique etc. Ceter<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> spero
      <lb/>brevi istuc perventur<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> Celeberrim<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-119166895" type="person">Agnat<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs>
      <lb/>Tu<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice>, qui summo meo, et omni<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> Amicor<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice>
      <lb/>dolore ante tres dies <rs key="place_GEO-3171728" type="place">Patavi<unclear><choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></unclear></rs> abiit illic discessurus
      <lb/>die <date when="1719-10-12">12 hujus mensis</date> et in <rs key="place_GEO-2661604" type="place">Patri<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice></rs> profecturus.
      <lb/>Ab ipsomet intelliges me omnia qu<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice> potui
      <lb/>fecisse ut <del>ips</del> ille permaneret <rs key="place_GEO-3171728" type="place">Patavii</rs> sed
      <lb/>frustra.</p> <closer><salute>Vale Vir Amicissime, mihique
      <lb/>favere ne desinas obsecro salutam plurim<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice>
      <lb/>dicendo <choice><abbr>Clariss.<hi rend="sup">o</hi></abbr><expan>Clarissimo</expan></choice> Filio Tuo <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Nicolao</rs>.</salute>
<dateline>Dabam
      <lb/><rs key="place_GEO-3164603" type="place">Venetiis</rs> <choice><abbr>a. d.</abbr><expan>ad diem</expan></choice> <date when="1719-10-06">6 Octobris 1719</date>.</dateline></closer>
